  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: mausoleum of Lollii</p>\r\n<p>R.J.A. Wilson notes that the mausoleum is located some 4 km north of Tiddis in isolated fields. Wilson debates whether Lollius and his family might have had an expansive country villa in the hinterland of Tiddis or not. (viz. Wilson in Marzano 2018: 270).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Quintus Lollius Urbicus served as a governor of Britannia between 139 and 142. His career is detailed on a pair of inscriptions from his hometown of Tiddis. His mausoleum is located a few kilometers north of Tiddis.",
